WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.167
-Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.434
You're here!
You made it.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:08.367
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:10.033
Well, guys,
I want to say congrats

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.634
to the Cincinnati Bengals
and Los Angeles Rams

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:15.334
on advancing to Super Bowl LVI.

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:16.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.367
-Wow!
-Before the season,

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:22.000
the Bengals' odds of winning
the Super Bowl were 150-1.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.767
-Ooh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.334
To give you an idea,
there are better odds

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:27.801
of finding a rapid test at CVS.
-Really?

00:00:27.801 --> 00:00:29.834
[ Laughter ]
Than going to the Super Bowl.

00:00:29.834 --> 00:00:31.634
-Wow!
[ Applause ]

00:00:31.634 --> 00:00:33.367
-That's true.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.367 --> 00:00:34.601
"I'm sorry."
-"Nope."

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.601
-"Nope."

00:00:36.601 --> 00:00:38.467
And this is crazy.
The Super Bowl is being played

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:41.701
in Los Angeles
at the Rams' home stadium.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.100
[ Cheers ]

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.133
That's right.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.334
Even NFL players
are working from home.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.767 --> 00:00:50.033
That's right.
We're two weeks away

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.834
from the game,
and experts are wondering,

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:54.234
if a Super Bowl doesn't have
Tom Brady,

00:00:54.234 --> 00:00:55.767
can it still be called
the Super Bowl?

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:57.834
I don't know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.234
I don't know.

00:00:59.234 --> 00:01:01.734
But this is the Bengals
first Super Bowl appearance

00:01:01.734 --> 00:01:04.234
since the '80s.
-Ooh.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.067
-A lot has changed since then.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:09.100
Back then, inflation was high,
there was tension with Russia,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.968
and our president
was in his late 70s.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:15.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.868 --> 00:01:18.167
Oh, and I saw that during
the Bengals/Chiefs games --

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:19.701
This just made me laugh.

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.901
Did you see the announcements
over at CBS?

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.534
-Oh, yeah.
-They have a great crew.

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.567
They're awesome over there.
But at CBS, they're doing

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.667
the halftime, talking about
the stats and all that stuff.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.834
But they were just
in the worst spot

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:33.534
you could possibly be
on the field to talk.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:34.767
But take a look
at the halftime report.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:35.767
Look at this.

00:01:35.767 --> 00:01:38.601
-...as we welcome
Grammy-nominated

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:42.033
singer-songwriter Walker Hayes!

00:01:42.033 --> 00:01:45.367
-...this game...
[ Country music plays loudly ]

00:01:45.367 --> 00:01:49.667
They score, they go down...
[ Country music plays loudly ]

00:01:49.667 --> 00:01:54.767
-At what point do you consider
blitzing Patrick Mahomes?

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.200
-I have no idea
what you just said.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.834
I can't hear a thing
anybody is saying.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:01:59.934
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.200
The speakers
are right behind them!

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:03.267
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:04.868
It's the first football game
where the announcers

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.400
got concussions.
Unbelievable.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.934 --> 00:02:10.234
You know the closed-captioning
guy was in a white-hot panic,

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.434
like, "I can't -- I don't --
I don't know what to --"

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.934 --> 00:02:16.667
It sounds like when your friend
calls you from every concert.

00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:18.601
Like, "Man, it's great!
Yeah!"

00:02:18.601 --> 00:02:20.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:22.033
When the music stopped,
Boomer Esiason

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:23.734
was still yelling
at full volume.

00:02:23.734 --> 00:02:26.067
"And that's why Mahomes has to
have more of a running game!"

00:02:26.067 --> 00:02:28.000
They go...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.267
Meanwhile, the big football
story form this weekend

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:31.934
wasn't the games.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:36.133
On Saturday, ESPN reported
that Tom Brady is retiring.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.400
But then --
[ Cheers ]

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.200
But then,
conflicting reports came out

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.767
that said
Brady hasn't decided yet.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:43.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:45.067
This is what happens
when you let the CDC

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.767
announce your retirement.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.634
You just don't know --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:53.033
6 feet, 3 feet, 5 days...

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:54.367
[ Applause ]

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.300
Brady was like, "I just
wanted to see who was happy

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.467
so I can destroy them."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:00.901
Let's switch gears.
Over the weekend,

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.801
former president Trump
held a rally in Texas

00:03:03.801 --> 00:03:05.968
where he talked about
running for President

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.334
and said that if he won,

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.667
he might pardon
the January 6th rioters.

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:11.734
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.267
Even the rioters were like,
"Oh, no,

00:03:13.267 --> 00:03:16.934
I don't think he can say that."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.934 --> 00:03:19.000
Yeah, there's no way --
no better way to announce

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.501
a presidential run than saying,
"I'll empty the jails."

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:26.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:29.701
Well, the East Coast
is recovering

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:32.167
from a massive blizzard
that hit this weekend.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:35.000
Boston actually got one of its
biggest snowstorms ever,

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.801
but that didn't stop people
from going out.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.033
Watch this.

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:39.467
-Have you heard the news
about Tom Brady?

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:42.300
-Yes.
-What do you make of all that?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.601
-I don't know.
I don't know.

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:45.367
Is Gronk next then, I guess?

00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:47.067
-I thought he had
a couple more years, maybe.

00:03:47.067 --> 00:03:48.667
-Where are you guys
trying to go right now?

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.601
-We're trying to find
an open Dunkin' Donuts.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.634
[ Rim shot ]
-Can't find them.

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.400
-Come on!
-No, dude --

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:58.801
-Come on!
-That's real.

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.801
-Oh, my God.

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.434
-We did not do anything
to that tape.

00:04:02.434 --> 00:04:05.100
That is real.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.667
Tom Brady, Dunkin' Donuts.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.434
If they snuck in David Ortiz,

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.367
they would have summoned
the ghost of Sam Adams.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:13.968
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:17.100
How Boston is that?
Fantastic.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.534
[ Applause ]

00:04:19.534 --> 00:04:21.400
You might have a problem
when you're willing to put on

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.601
ski goggles just to get
a pineapple Coolatta.

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:26.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.400
But they weren't the only ones

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.734
who braved
the weekend's blizzard.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:30.234
I saw that a couple
in Rhode Island

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:33.467
actually got married outside
during the storm.

00:04:33.467 --> 00:04:35.200
Here's the happy couple there
right there.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.167
Yeah.
And this is real.

00:04:37.167 --> 00:04:39.901
Here's everyone
who showed up to the wedding.

00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:42.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:44.367
You know it's cold when your
"something blue"

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.667
are your guests.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:48.868
And finally, a man who lives
on a lake in Canada

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.400
snapped a photo of a figure
that formed when waves

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:53.901
splashed onto the shore
and froze around a lamp post.

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:55.467
People are saying it looks like
the Grim Reaper.

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:56.934
Take a look at this.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.467
-Ooh.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.033
-Everyone thought it was
the Grim Reaper

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.701
until they heard grandpa
whisper, "Help. Help me."

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:05.634 --> 00:05:09.234
Hey, did you guys hear about
the Nissan recall?

00:05:09.234 --> 00:05:11.167
It's not good.
Here, check this out.

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:13.267
-A massive recall alert
to tell you about.

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:16.467
Nissan is recalling
more than 793,000

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:20.067
small SUVs in the U.S. because
water can get into the wiring

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:22.300
and, in rare cases,
could start a fire.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:23.634
-What?

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:28.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:30.300
A fire?

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.133
-Oh, hey,
it's Tariq Trotter, everybody.

00:05:32.133 --> 00:05:35.400
Tariq!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.767
What are you doing out here?

00:05:36.767 --> 00:05:39.267
Your interview isn't until
later in the show?

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:41.033
-Well, no,
I just bought a Nissan,

00:05:41.033 --> 00:05:43.634
so I heard you talking about it,
and I rushed out here.

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.167
-Yeah, well,
sorry about the recall.

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:49.133
-It's fine. Look, I still have
my trusty Hyundai.

00:05:49.133 --> 00:05:51.834
It's one of their
newer vehicles.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:54.434
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:56.300
-"Oh" what?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:57.767
-Roll the clip.

00:05:57.767 --> 00:06:01.534
-Hyundai sounds the alarm about
three of its newer vehicles.

00:06:01.534 --> 00:06:03.133
There's an issue
with the windshield

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:06.033
that can cause it to break off
while driving.

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:08.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.701
-Break off?

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.167
Come on, that's insane.

00:06:11.167 --> 00:06:13.534
-Yeah, I'm sorry about that,
Tariq.

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:15.767
-Man, I can't handle
any more bad news.

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:17.968
-There's got to be something
that you're looking forward to.

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:21.234
-I mean,
I am excited for lunch tomorrow.

00:06:21.234 --> 00:06:23.601
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, I bought a bunch of this

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:25.534
really good
vegan mac and cheese.

00:06:25.534 --> 00:06:27.968
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.968 --> 00:06:29.701
It's in my pantry.

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:30.801
-And check your pantry.

00:06:30.801 --> 00:06:32.767
It's listed as
vegan mac and cheese,

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:36.467
but it's not actually vegan,
and it might even be dangerous.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:37.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.934 --> 00:06:40.267
-Dangerous?

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:42.000
-You should probably
throw it out.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.634
-What else do I even have
in my kitchen right now?

00:06:44.634 --> 00:06:47.501
Just a bag
of frozen chopped spinach.

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:51.200
-Recall alert -- this time
for frozen chopped spinach.

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.100
-Come on.
You know what?

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:56.400
Forget it.
I'm just gonna sit back

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.868
and relax on my new beach chair.

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:02.234
I got one in light blue
and another one in red.

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:06.801
-We've got a recall alert
in that specific beach chair.

00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:08.467
Where you probably bought it,

00:07:08.467 --> 00:07:10.400
and why you should
stop using it.

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:12.734
-Man, I'm getting so mad!
Man, I just want to --

00:07:12.734 --> 00:07:15.033
I just want to take
a chainsaw and go berserk.

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.234
-Well, wait, wait!
Hold up.

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:19.434
What kind of chainsaw?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.434 --> 00:07:27.234
-Well, I have a Dewalt DWCS600
18-inch corded chainsaw.

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:32.901
-More than 8,000 Dewalt DWCS600
18-inch corded chainsaws

00:07:32.901 --> 00:07:34.000
are being recalled.

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.934
-That's it, man!
I'm done!

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:37.868
I am done!
[ Chainsaw motor whirring ]

00:07:37.868 --> 00:07:41.667
-Tariq -- Tariq is gonna cool
down before his interview.

00:07:41.667 --> 00:07:44.234
His musical, "Black No More,"
is playing now

00:07:44.234 --> 00:07:45.634
though February 27th

00:07:45.634 --> 00:07:47.601
at the Pershing Square
Signature Center.

00:07:47.601 --> 00:07:49.234
Stick around.
We'll be right back,

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:50.801
with "Puppy Predictors."

